<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

  <!--
    SCALD_DIVING_MOD_1's ONLY reference to the Scald by name — data wiring,
    not lore (About.xml). Tags the three Standable RUT_ScaldWater* terrains
    (WaterShallowBase/WaterChestDeepBase descendants — pathCost 30/42, no
    passability override, so they default Standable) with the generic
    RM_DiveEligible tag this mod's float menu and job drivers key on.

    Deliberately EXCLUDES RUT_ScaldWaterDeep and RUT_ScaldWaterOceanDeep:
    those are WaterDeepBase descendants (passability Impassable,
    Core/Defs/TerrainDefs/Terrain_Water.xml line 78-79, verified this
    session) — a walking pawn cannot path onto them regardless of any tag,
    so the boiling SURFACE stays structurally no-swim (the_scald.md ban 4).
    RM_DiveUtility.CellIsDiveSite's own Standable() check is the redundant
    second gate if a future biome ever tags impassable terrain by mistake.

    MayRequire guards every operation: absent mandrake.rut.patches (the
    Scald was never built, or a player has no Utinni content at all), this
    patch does nothing and this mod ships fully inert but intact — the
    "medieval-tribe player installs this alone" test in About.xml.
  -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd" MayRequire="mandrake.rut.patches">
    <xpath>/Defs/TerrainDef[defName="RUT_ScaldWaterShallow"]/tags</xpath>
    <value>
      <li>RM_DiveEligible</li>
    </value>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd" MayRequire="mandrake.rut.patches">
    <xpath>/Defs/TerrainDef[defName="RUT_ScaldWaterMovingShallow"]/tags</xpath>
    <value>
      <li>RM_DiveEligible</li>
    </value>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd" MayRequire="mandrake.rut.patches">
    <xpath>/Defs/TerrainDef[defName="RUT_ScaldWaterMovingChestDeep"]/tags</xpath>
    <value>
      <li>RM_DiveEligible</li>
    </value>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
